From: Nabu Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: reset inbound state only on subsystem restart

The SMP2P v2 support clears each inbound entry's last_value even when the
restart-done flag matches the acknowledged state. Ordinary notifications
then replay every asserted bit as a rising edge. On nabu, SLPI notifications
with slave-kernel == 0x6 repeatedly dispatch ready and handover, producing
"Handover signaled, but it already happened" at the sensor notification rate.

Preserve edge history unless a restart is actually pending. Keep resetting
it on a real restart so v2 peers that reassert bits before the SSR ack are
still handled.

This regression is present in the pinned mainline kernel; the 6.17 sm8150
fork predates the reset loop and does not need this patch.

---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -194,6 +194,10 @@ static bool qcom_smp2p_check_ssr(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
 
 	restart_done = in->flags & BIT(SMP2P_FLAGS_RESTART_DONE_BIT);
 	restart = restart_done != smp2p->ssr_ack;
+	if (!restart)
+		return false;
+
+	/* Replay asserted bits only after a remote subsystem restart. */
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
 		if (!entry->value)
 			continue;
